id: pm-vcs-hre2
title: Publication refuses without a valid stable-FileId lock lease
description: "Publication refuses without a valid stable FileId lease at the receiver ref transaction. Missing, expired, wrong-principal and out-of-scope leases have distinct typed refusals with FileId, holder and expiry diagnostics. Explicit authenticated acquisition, renewal, release and administrator break use durable fenced generations across rename and process boundaries. Implementation and regression evidence are linked; package validation and review receipts are maintained in PR #100, and this item stays open."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-28T13:43:14.894Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T14:47:44.846Z"
author: pi-agent
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-5h6j,parent,"2026-08-28T15:22:45.240Z",claude,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[29]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T20:11:19.721Z",pi-agent,"PR #48 review confirmed this acceptance criterion is intentionally not implemented. The branch contains no publication lock-lease implementation or passing acceptance evidence for this child, so it remains open with its written specification."
  "2026-09-12T23:35:49.681Z",pi-agent,"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — nothing. The description says spec only. grep for lease/Lease/stable-FileId in engine/ returns no matches. No lock lease implementation exists. REMAINS — the full feature: publication refusal for missing, expired, wrong-principal, or out-of-scope lock leases, with four distinct named refusals."
  "2026-10-11T05:07:14.215Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator read the merged architecture and feature specification. One integrated implementation will enforce stable FileId leases at the receiver publication boundary, with distinct missing, expired, wrong-principal and branch-scope refusals, and real process race evidence. Independent review and verification follow before one unmerged PR."
  "2026-10-11T05:11:14.381Z",codex-sol,"Plan: receiver-owned FileId generations and fencing proofs, durable lease audit, explicit acquire/renew/release/break workflows, and enforcement inside the shared receiver write lock immediately before ref CAS. Cover filesystem and authenticated HTTP plus real process races; keep both feature items open for independent review."
  "2026-10-11T05:26:03.973Z",codex-agent,Independent review requested publication-versus-lease mutation/expiry process races and batch atomic refusal evidence beyond acquisition contention. Private proof storage must safely handle valid remote names that collide with object prototype properties. The implementation remains under review; no merge or closure is authorized.
  "2026-10-11T05:32:45.838Z",codex-sol,"Review correction: proof registries now use own-property reads and safe writes for valid prototype-like remote names. Added independent publisher processes paused before receiver publication and independent renew/release/break operations, receiver-clock expiry, batch refusal, and historical create-then-delete identity scenarios. No production push path acquires leases automatically."
  "2026-10-11T05:52:05.715Z",codex-agent,Independent review corrected lease audit directory flushing to reuse syncDirectory with the same supported-platform behavior as private control metadata. Event-file fsync remains mandatory; supported directory flushing follows it. This avoids introducing an ordinary lease-operation failure on platforms where Node cannot open directory descriptors. The Linux lease scenarios remain behaviorally unchanged; final gates will cover the integrated change.
  "2026-10-11T05:55:52.787Z",codex-sol,"Expanded receiver scenarios passed 9/9 with zero skips: acquisition contention; independent paused publication versus renew, release, break and receiver expiry; rename continuity; stale fence after reacquisition; batch refusal leaving both refs unchanged; and historical create-then-delete identity refusal. Real tracker/SDK workflows passed for __proto__, constructor and toString remotes. Packed and process consumers are being updated with explicit fixture leases; production push still acquires none. Paged erasure now inspects lease audit storage for retained payload copies."
  "2026-10-11T06:07:35.008Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral lease proof: removed only RefStore.transaction preflight invocation after CAS validation and before original ref writes; ran node --test test/publication-leases.test.ts against native TypeScript source. The nine scenarios produced seven expected behavioral failures (missing/ownership/scope or deletion refusal, independent release/break/expiry, and batch refusal accepted when enforcement was absent), two unaffected controls passed, zero skipped. Restored the exact saved transaction function and rebuilt before restored verification. Exploratory whole-suite execution also exposed packed/process consumers requiring explicit fixture leases, now corrected. Several unchanged one-second or ten-second baseline process deadlines fail under host contention; deadlines and coverage thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-11T06:30:38.264Z",codex-agent,"Independent orchestrator verification: node --test test/lease-workflows.test.ts passed 1/1 with zero failures, cancellations or skips. Real SDK tracker and installed compiled extension workflows acquired, pushed, inspected, renewed and released explicit leases for __proto__, constructor and toString remote names. The CLI fixture uses a long valid lifetime for process startup; dedicated expired-lease refusal scenarios retain their short lifetimes. Final full release gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-11T06:40:19.236Z",codex-sol,"Latest focused native-source verification passed 31/31 tests across feature edges and publication lease scenarios, with zero failures, cancellations or skips. This includes newly added request validation and nested stable FileIds with anonymous legacy-tree compatibility. Linked PM test execution and unchanged full coverage gate are underway; earlier measured and behavioral revert evidence remains preserved."
  "2026-10-11T06:41:19.091Z",codex-sol,"Required linked execution passed: pm test pm-vcs-hre2 --run --progress ran node --test test/publication-leases.test.ts test/lease-workflows.test.ts, 11/11 passed, zero failed, cancelled, skipped or todo; exit 0. Real compiled extension and SDK tracker exercised prototype-like remotes. Full unchanged coverage gate remains underway; no confirmed PM CLI or SDK defect has been reproduced."
  "2026-10-11T06:58:24.660Z",codex-sol,"Readiness hardening: real peer IPC waits now have bounded message deadlines and reject process exit before readiness or a result; the existing served pusher also rejects a clean early exit. After this test-only change, pm test pm-vcs-hre2 --run --progress again passed 11/11, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo, exit 0. Current full-suite exploration contains baseline process deadline failures under shared contention; the two audit cases rechecked PASS at their original one-second limits. No deadline, source coverage threshold, dependency or version was changed."
  "2026-10-11T07:01:57.534Z",codex-sol,"Gate fixture correction: shared load near fifty across four CPUs caused installed CLI scenario watchdog exhaustion and older ten-second process startup failures. Test-only composition child watchdogs now allow 120 seconds, and the multi-command installed consumer allows 900 seconds. Audit startup watchdogs allow 30 seconds while the intentional 20ms timeout remains unchanged. Served multi-process and serial CLI fixtures now allow their actual startup costs. Engine lock, lease and transport timeouts, deliberate short-expiry tests, memory ceilings, behavior assertions, coverage thresholds and source inventory are unchanged. The interrupted exploratory coverage log and raw data were preserved; isolated failing cases are being rechecked before fresh full coverage."
  "2026-10-11T07:04:22.151Z",codex-sol,"Isolated watchdog regression verification passed 11/11, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo: node --test --test-reporter=tap --test-name-pattern=\"stream transport|restore, sparse materialization|self-targeted pin|review denials reuse|review short owner|renewed no-op fetch|renewed links read|renewed scan and status|renewed live writer|renewal closure discards\" test/audit-git-identities.test.ts test/composition.test.ts. Native closure retained original bounds: 134217728 leaf bytes, 72 reachable objects read once, 136361605 compressed bytes, 21039136 buffer growth and 14680064 native peak RSS growth. Fresh complete unchanged coverage execution follows the interrupted exploratory run."
  "2026-10-11T07:06:08.849Z",codex-sol,"Installed consumer recheck passed: node --test --test-reporter=tap test/composition-consumer.test.ts, 1/1 passed, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo; 245259ms total. All five scenarios succeeded, including project-installed CLI after the four built/packed Node/Bun SDK scenarios. The previous 120-second installed-scenario watchdog was shorter than actual serial startup and install cost; only the test watchdog changed to 900 seconds. Original publication, secret, merge, erasure and real SDK assertions remain."
  "2026-10-11T07:20:09.639Z",codex-sol,"Real served fixture verification passed: node --test --test-reporter=tap test/served-acceptance.test.ts test/served-defects.test.ts, 5/5 passed, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo; 772556ms total. Both Node and Bun packed global CLI scenarios retained secret protection, explicit lease preparation, stale refusal, merge and all-store verification. The Node scenario alone needed 276057ms, confirming the former 240-second test watchdog was insufficient for actual startup cost. These are fixture budgets, with production deadlines and intentional expiry unchanged."
  "2026-10-11T07:33:50.993Z",codex-sol,"Final linked integration execution passed: pm test pm-vcs-hre2 --run --progress ran both commands with exit 0. Lease and real SDK workflow command: 11/11 passed, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo (76981ms). Consumer command node --test test/composition-consumer.test.ts test/served-acceptance.test.ts test/served-defects.test.ts: 6/6 passed, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo (614702ms). All real Node/Bun packed and installed CLI assertions remain. Tracker test-result policy is unchanged; passing receipts are recorded here. Complete coverage and committed-HEAD release gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-11T07:51:03.407Z",codex-agent,"Independent full-suite review found two successful raw HTTP upload-session publication fixtures without lease proofs. Added explicit real HttpTransport acquisition for each seeded stable FileId, scoped to main, and carried those proofs in the publication JSON. The session eviction, cumulative object/byte charge, refusal and receipt-reset assertions are unchanged; production publication still acquires no leases. Two isolated session tests are being verified. Shared-object read-once production integration remains under the implementation agent review."
  "2026-10-11T07:51:22.988Z",codex-sol,"Full-suite diagnosis found duplicate commit/tree reads after closure validation, plus measurement setup acquiring leases inside the read counter and a fixture transaction wrapper dropping the authoritative preflight. Publication now reuses receiver-validated structural metadata only under the uninterrupted object writer lease; leaf payload bytes are not retained. The fixture acquires explicit proofs before measurement and forwards preflight. node --test --test-reporter=tap test/publication-validation.test.ts passed 7/7, zero failures, cancellations, skips or todo; each shared object is read once under one writer lease. Continuing the surviving complete coverage run to collect remaining failures and coverage gaps."
  "2026-10-11T07:58:03.116Z",codex-agent,"Independent session fixture verification: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"an upload session is bounded|one reused upload\" test/serve.test.ts passed 2/2, zero failures, cancellations or skips, with real explicit receiver lease acquisition. Session eviction, cumulative receipt/object/byte limits and post-publication reset assertions are unchanged."
  "2026-10-11T07:59:16.177Z",codex-sol,"The surviving diagnostic npm run coverage completed 1417 tests: 1406 passed, 11 failed, zero cancellations/skips/todo, with 99.54 statements/lines, 98.18 branches and 99.48 functions. This mixed-source diagnostic is not a passing gate. Actual failures were explicit fixture authority omissions, test-helper class identity assertions, unknown-remote/unknown-branch setup masking production diagnostics, source inventory and registration counts, plus the fixed shared-read regression. Isolated session cases pass 2/2; served factory/force rollback pass 2/2; diagnostic/registration cases pass 4/4. No behavior assertion, production deadline, deliberate expiry, heap bound, source exclusion or coverage threshold was lowered. Refreshed linked lease run passed 11/11 and integration run 6/6, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo. Collecting fresh focused coverage to resolve remaining gaps before the unchanged full gates."
  "2026-10-11T08:11:41.417Z",codex-sol,"Final linked execution after all receiver-boundary and fixture corrections passed both registered commands via pm test pm-vcs-hre2 --run --progress: lease/CLI tests 11/11 and installed built/packed/served integrations 6/6, zero failures, cancellations, skips or todo, exit 0 for both. Tests preserve readiness rejection on early child exit, explicit fixture leases for observed old and new FileIds, unchanged intentional expiry and behavioral assertions. Production push paths never acquire leases automatically. Source/test typecheck, lint, duplicates and all 327 docstrings pass; the fresh complete coverage run remains pending."
  "2026-10-11T08:40:30.983Z",codex-sol,"Fresh complete coverage passed all 1418 tests with zero failures, cancellations, skips or todo; statements/functions/lines reached 100, branches were 99.93, so this was not a passing coverage gate. Four branches remained: two unused materializing paths in the private CDC buffer helper (all production callers provide incremental sinks), and shared-hub lease authority in linked FileTransport receivers. Removed only the obsolete private helper option and added a real linked acquisition/publication/release test verifying the hub audit and shared refs. Its first focused attempt passed the wrong root as the transport path and failed the hub audit assertion; correcting that fixture passed 1/1. A fresh unchanged complete coverage run and both linked commands are underway."
  "2026-10-11T09:03:00.423Z",codex-sol,"Complete unchanged npm run coverage passed: 1419/1419 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo, and 100/100/100/100 statements/branches/functions/lines across all 58 production files. Linked pm test --run --progress passed lease/CLI 11/11 and built/packed/served integrations 6/6 after final branch fixes, zero skips. Real multi-process acquisition and publication versus renewal, release, break and expiry are covered; refused batches, historical create-then-delete identities, renames and stale fences leave refs unchanged. Ref CAS preflight-only behavioral revert failed seven of nine lease cases (two controls passed); restoring it passed the focused suite, and current complete coverage passes. Source/test typecheck, lint, zero duplicates and 327 docstrings pass. No confirmed PM CLI/SDK defect was found. Releasing the claim while keeping this item in_progress/open for orchestrator review. Final steps are changelog regeneration, explicit staging, build, self-host bundle regeneration, SteveBot commit, committed-HEAD self-host verification and npm/Bun/isolated-identity release gates; final HEAD gate counts will be reported without another tracker mutation."
  "2026-10-11T09:28:24.372Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator took over final verification from the implementation worker. Publication preflight, durable generations and lease race proofs are unchanged. The first package gate found one streaming-buffer margin failure; the manifest feature now uses a 32 KiB output buffer and all package gates will run again at the next frozen commit."
  "2026-10-11T09:35:35.505Z",codex-sol,"After the first HEAD npm gate reported one narrow restore buffer assertion failure (1418/1419 passed; 100/100/100/100 source coverage, zero skips), reduced actual streaming output allocation from 64 to 32 KiB without changing budgets or assertions. Refreshed pm test pm-vcs-hre2 --run --progress passed lease/CLI 11/11 and built/packed/served integrations 6/6, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo. Manifest linked checks also pass 31/31, 55/55 and 80/80. Publication ownership, receiver-clock expiry, fencing and atomic preflight are unchanged; root audit directory synchronization remains. Releasing the claim again while leaving this item in_progress/open. Final tracker writes precede changelog, bundle regeneration and the correction commit; all three required complete release gates will be rerun against that committed unchanged HEAD."
  "2026-10-11T09:36:50.853Z",codex-agent,"Implementation, real process races, typed diagnostics and behavioral preflight revert evidence are linked in this item and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/100. The linked lease and installed/served integration commands passed 11 of 11 and 6 of 6, zero failures or skips. Package validation and review receipts are maintained in that PR. This item remains open after claim release."
  "2026-10-11T14:47:44.845Z",claude-hub,"Review fixes: (1) publication walks skip every commit reachable from the replaced tip, so a merge parent that bypasses expected no longer drags published history (and lease demands for long-deleted FileIds) into the check; (2) lease inspect returns the fencing token only to the holder, other principals see generation:000.. ; (3) closure dedup keys use scalar fields plus the parent's content address instead of the parent's full page list. Regressions in test/publication-leases.test.ts; reverting (1) fails with lease_missing, reverting (2) fails the HTTP principal test."
